// deathtips_data.acs — built-in death tips + registration (fragment).
// Included by deathtips.acs AFTER the registry API; declares no library.
//
// Every built-in tip is one UH_RegisterTip call below: text, byline ("" = use
// the pool byline), wrap width (0 = default 220), pool and weight.  This
// replaces the former compile-time arrays — the strings now sit next to their
// metadata instead of in a parallel array you have to cross-reference, and
// adding a tip is a single line.  Text, bylines, wrap widths and weights are
// transcribed verbatim from the former tables; do not "fix" spacing or color
// codes.
//
// Demoneye quotes
// Idea stolen from LMSGames who stole it from Internal Conflict
//
// Weights: UH_TIP_WEIGHT_DEFAULT for the normal rotation, UH_TIP_WEIGHT_404 for
// the joke row, 0 for parked rows (registered, never drawn).  Selection is
// weighted over all rows, so pools only decide bylines.
//
// Registration runs once per map on every client (map arrays are zeroed on
// every map load).  The engine also forwards CLIENTSIDE OPEN scripts from the
// server, so this may run twice per client — UH_RegisterTip dedupes, which is
// also why no UHInPlay() guard is needed here.


// --- built-in registration ---------------------------------------------------
function void UH_RegisterBuiltinTips(void) {
  // --- The Luser (UH_POOL_THELUSER, 16 rows) --------------------------------
